EFFICIENCY:

- Alternative implementation using coarrays

  Workers (images 2 to n) simulate the trajectories and deliver the 
  projectiles with tasks (put_eval_task). Image 1 scores the projectiles
  in moments, histograms, and cells (eval**). Workers get current state of 
  histograms and cells after each collision cascade as needed.
  
  put_eval_task puts the tasks into a queue. Implementation of a queue see,
  e.g. [Rei09] Ch.12.4, or [Bra15] Ch.12.4.

- Alternative implementation using OpenMP

  Using tasks, avoiding breakup of work into equal number of collision cascades.  

- In order to avoid application of the rotation matrix to each atom of the
  search cell, the search cubes should store the atom positions in the
  target coordinate system. Then only the origin of the coordinate system 
  needs to be rotated and the atom coordinates just be added.

  This requires to know about the lattice vectors (defined in mat) in the
  xtal modules. Thus, the search cube must be defined for each region 
  separately. (-> probably this change is reasonable only when multiple
  crystal structures are implemented)

- In order to eliminate the extra time spent with the larger search cells
  (diamond search cell has now alat instead of alat/4 as edge length), one
  could define search cells as subcells of the lattice unit cell, e.g.
  by specifying the number of subdivisions for each edge of the unit cell.
  (-> probably this change should be done together with the implementation 
  of multiple crstalline regions, such search cells could possibly go beyond 
  the current region)

- Initialization of distance function according to Mau00. In a second step, 
  use quadtree where larger distances use smaller resolution. This will be 
  essential for 3D.

- Cascade evaluation using quadtree. (?)

- Optimize NRAD2 as a function of energy

