DONE (2023-10):
==============

IMPLEMENTED FEATURES:

- (2024-01-22) Parallel version using OpenMP. 
               Advantages: Serial version in the same code, also working with gfortran.

- (2023-08-21) Parallel version using coarrays.

- (2023-06-09) SRIM-2013 electronic stopping powers as an option.

- (2023-02-28) Second tilt angle (TILTY).

USER INTERFACE:

- (2022-06-15) Rename input parameters FIL*** and ***FIL to ***FILE.
 
- (2022-06-07) Replace character arrays with simple arrays. As a consequence, quotation marks
  have to be omitted when specifying former character arrays. Character arrays were introduced,
  since before Fortran 2003 allocatable arrays were not allowed to be part of namelists.
  However, this could have been circumvented by allowing multiple records for the same
  namelist and joining the values of the same parameter specified on different records. This 
  has now been realized (even though allocatable arrays are now allowed to be part of 
  namelists).
  
- (2022-05-27) 2-D geometry definition with region 0 definition optional.

- (2022-05-20) Make background execution the default in imsil.py script.

- (2022-05-20) Avoid writing '../' in file paths specified in the input file. This is done by 
  introducing another path variable inppath in the PATH file. Now input files are searched for 
  first in the working directory, then in the original directory of the input file, and finally
  in the tables directory.

- (2022-05-19) Allow z<-1mm and z>10mm in HIS file. This may happen for MeV H implants.

- (2022-05-18) In statistics output (OUT file), make precision at least good enough to resolve 
  10 times the uncertainty.

MAJOR BUG FIXES (those that were a TODO previously):

- (BUGFIX: 2023-08-16) FFPMIN was not reset after a free flight path without collision. This
  could lead to increased ion ranges in dynamic simulations. 

- (BUGFIX: 2023-02-14) Parents of virtual recoils were considered to be created in
  subthreshold collision when they have stopped. This can lead to stopping of the program in 
  static simulations for parents that are ions because damage is tried to be calculated for 
  subthreshold atoms. Ions are now excluded from conversion to subthreshold.

- (BUGFIX: 2022-09-01) Histograms were incorrectly read using USEHIS when the boxes were 
  non-matching with the grid specified in the input file.

- (BUGFIX: 2022-08-18) The statistical error in interstitial and vacancy characteristics was 
  largely underestimated, since all I and V were treated as being generated independently of 
  each other. Moreover, the error of skewness and kurtosis have been estimated under the
  assumption that the standard deviation is without error. Both assumptions are not correct.
  These bugs were fixed by new theory. 

- (BUGFIX: 2022-05-12) Seed of random number generator was ineffective for Knuth. After
  fixing this bug, all simulations now run with different statistics.

- (BUGFIX: 2022-03-25) The average local electronic stopping for impact parameters > pmax was 
  calculated incorrectly in an amorphous region if the ffp cylinder intersects a neighboring 
  region because the pmax of the neighboring region was considered if the ffp in the neighboring 
  region is smaller than the ffp in the current region. This was particularly severe if the 
  neighboring region is crystalline (thus the pmax=pmaxc being large) and the pmax in the 
  current region is small (i.e., at high energies).
  
  The critical part of the code is in selncp.f90:139 (in the if(ffp2<ffp) block). This sets the
  pmax which is later used in the evaluation of the electronic energy loss. See
  ~/work/imsil/stable/projects/smit/H.


