CODE DESIGN:

- (this has at least partially been realized) We presently have eval_stat_mod 
  which has defined (among others) histogram objects of the changes to the 
  target. The histogram classes are defined in stat_his*d_mod. 

  Similarly, we should have eval_det_mod which has defined a DefectColumn 
  object. eval_det_mod should contain several of the xtal_lsatoms_det_mod
  subroutines:
	det10 (in order to initialize from a histogram, a temporary 
               histogram object has to be created)
	getLSAtomsDet (-> det60)
	det23 (atom/vacancy added to Column)
	det30
	his30 (calling det2his ?)
	createGrid ?
	createLattice ?
	strain
	strainDef
  In addition a	det21 subroutine should be written that takes into account
  that atoms/vacancies may be taken away from Column

  his10 (-> det2his) should go into eval_stat_mod (generate a temporary
  DefectColumn object?)

  The DefectColumn class should be defined in a new module det_column_mod 
  which is an extension of the present def_readwrite_mod. Some of the 
  procedures of xtal_lsatoms_det_mod would go into det_column_mod:
	dethis10 (-> det2his)
	getCol (-> getColBnd)
	balanceDef
	getIndices

BUGS:

- rrobin stops with rrobin (?) if array bounds are checked (i.e. with the 
  debug version).

- usegeom=t of &setup leads to attempting writing out geom%posif before it
  is allocated. usegeom has been deactivated sometimes between 2003 and 2007.
  It was used to read the regions' geometry definition from the BCK file. It
  probably makes sense only when the region geometry is changed during the
  simulation, i.e., when mat(:)%syield /= 0.

MISC:

- cell1d, eval30: out%his -> dam%ldam
  edam in cell1d

- introduction of Ipos_type has slowed down the code by 20% (rbs2) to 100% 
  (rrobin) => should be eliminated again, requires deterministic defects
  in arbitrary crystal structures.

- in selncc, the region is checked with the atom positions which may include 
  lattice vibrations. This will lead to 50% of the first atom layer to be lost
  if posif is exactly at that layer. Can be avoided by the user by slightly 
  moving posif. Can be avoided by the programmer by introducing site%pos and 
  doing the region check with site instead of atom.

- Deterministic Si defects will probably never be used. When eliminating them, they could 
  be replaced by external big unit cells of a crystal, if one doesn't like to loose the 
  functionality.


